From b148834e6dd85927b824206fcc44839a95ce987b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@lmepisowifi.local>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 01:55:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Sync from tmwim2-2050-g40 (13 commits since fork point
 dc5de9c, M2 v1.5.32 -> v1.5.38)

Ports forward everything M2 gained that PGN6401V's hardware also supports:

  - QoS rework in lmehspt.sh: per-user Band1/Band2 real HTB rate limiting
    (replaces the old unbounded strict-priority prio qdisc), rate-scaled
    SFQ queue limits, DSCP EF/AF41 classification, and a tc -batch fast
    path for Equal Bandwidth Sharing rebalancing
  - ota.sh: backgrounded fetch() with a 60s-stall watchdog and a jsDelivr
    mirror (url_mirror) for the base bundle, fixing OTA hangs on ISPs
    that black-hole release-assets.githubusercontent.com; adds the
    .ota_heal_seen_<NAME> one-shot guard so self_heal() can't keep
    resurrecting a setting the admin already cleared
  - module_ctl.sh: gc_legacy_assets() to finish/redo the modules/<id>.assets
    -> hotspot_data/ migration on every reconcile instead of only at
    install time
  - www2/cgi-bin/lme.cgi: dashboard CPU-usage sampling now diffs against
    the previous action=dynamic poll instead of blocking each request on
    a manufactured 1s /proc/stat window (removes a recurring CPU spike)
  - RELOAD_AFTER_TIME_ADDED_ENABLED admin toggle (Session Settings) that
    forces a page reload after coin/voucher success or a resume, for
    devices whose captive-portal prompt won't self-close otherwise
  - Auto-Resume no longer resumes a manually-paused (Kick / customer
    Pause Time) session: new per-MAC auto_paused.txt marker set only by
    lmehspt.sh's inactivity watchdog and cleared at every manual
    pause/resume/removal site
  - www2/httpd.conf (new) + startup.sh: .woff/.woff2 MIME types for
    BusyBox httpd, fixing intermittent missing Content-Type on fonts;
    nav.js is loaded via a plain <script src> tag instead of a
    document.write cache-buster (blank-page fix)
  - release.yml: publishes a jsDelivr-mirrored copy of the base bundle
    tarball (dist/, force-added) alongside manifest.txt/modules.txt

Deliberately NOT ported (PGN6401V hardware doesn't support these; PGN
removed the equivalents from its own tree back in aead9b1 and never
carried them forward through any merge since):

  - www2/wlanlimit.html (WLAN access-limit page)
  - www2/services.html + the ipacl.cgi-derived remote/local access-control
    section it hosts (the "ipacl page")

manifest.txt / modules.txt conflicts resolved in favor of PGN's own
existing values (version, repo URL, sha256) - both files are written by
release CI (see file header) and will be regenerated correctly, with
real checksums, the next time PGN's own release.yml runs.

M2's own dist/*.tar.gz build artifacts (wrong-device firmware) were not
carried over; PGN's own CI will produce its own under the updated
release.yml.

PGN's pre-existing 4-ethernet-port carve-out in hotspot.cgi's
ifaces_get (eth0.2.0-eth0.5.0) was untouched by this sync - none of the
13 source commits touch that whitelist.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
